  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In the following reactions, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">R</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">S</mi></math> are the major products.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/c9bb0164-a0e9-4b52-bc31-e17ae6941330.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 72px;\" /></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/bdb5721b-6a26-41aa-b566-0d0a4e7786c4.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 103px;\" /></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/7d2638fe-87f9-4200-9c28-c1bb08fd1778.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 82px;\" /></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/68d2c70a-8e9c-4fbd-a310-5c0124fc2fd6.png\" style=\"width: 309px; height: 110px;\" /></p><p>The correct statement about <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">R</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">S</mi></math> is</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "OXVAm",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">P</mi></math> is a primary alcohol with four carbons.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "q8DbU",
      "text": "Q undergoes Kolbe&#39;s electrolysis to give an eight-carbon product.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "P7fu6",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">R</mi></math> has six carbons and it undergoes Cannizzaro reaction.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PZtXb",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">S</mi></math> is a primary amine with six carbons.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The isobutyl chloride on reaction with magnesium metal in dry ether give respective Grignard reagent. Grignard reagents produce hydrocarbon on reaction with water.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/75b195ea-46a4-4b17-8b4b-99eaa8009589.png\" style=\"width: 550px; height: 124px;\" /></p><p>Grignard reagent can react with carbon dioxide and acidic water to give respective carboxylic acid. Carboxylic acid gives carboxylate with sodium hydroxide.This salt of carboxylic acid undergo Kolbe&#39;s electrolysis to give hydrocarbon as shown below.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/c7dd82ba-040d-446a-aca2-e0c6383f0c46.png\" style=\"width: 650px; height: 286px;\" /></p><p>Kolbe electrolysis :</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/312613c7-74b0-4d54-8613-f3175d7a7330.png\" style=\"width: 526px; height: 154px;\" /></p><p>The two isobutyl radicals formed in the above reaction combines to give a hydrocarbon that contain eight carbons.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/3f93326b-06e7-44ea-9351-b87c73fcebc7.png\" style=\"width: 576px; height: 135px;\" /></p><p>The Grignard reagent formed from isobutyl chloride, reacts with acetaldehyde give respective secondary alcohol, which undergo oxidation with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CrO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;gives ketone as shown below.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/55340852-3dba-4df4-8090-bfcac6217cb0.png\" style=\"width: 550px; height: 314px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The above product undergoes aldol condensation reaction but&nbsp;not Cannizzaro&#39;s reaction.</p><p>The isobutyl chloride gives isobutyl cyanide on reaction with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ethanolic</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>NaCN</mi></math>. The cyanide undergo reduction with hydrogen in nickel gives primary amine. The primary amine formed undergo carbyl amine reaction gives isocyanide. The isocyanide gives secondary amine with lithium aluminium hydride.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/0c5ee779-1dc1-4cb6-bf4b-b8d44c85dbb3.png\" style=\"width: 706px; height: 467px;\" /></p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
